        "severity": "critical",
        "evidence": "The proof claims 'The trace and volume map are linear on the Hecke algebra', allowing it to write $\\mathrm{Vol}(\\overline{\\gamma}) = \\mathrm{Vol}(\\overline{1}) + \\sum \\phi_i \\mathrm{Vol}(\\overline{\\sigma_i})$. This is a mathematically false claim. Hyperbolic volume is a highly non-linear geometric invariant of the link complement; it does not extend linearly across linear combinations in the Hecke algebra.",
